.TH TULPAR-REPO 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.1.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-repo \- manage configured repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar repo add
.I url
.RI [ \-\-user ]
.br
.B tulpar repo remove
.I url
.RI [ \-\-user ]
.br
.B tulpar repo list
.br
.B tulpar repo update
.br
.B tulpar e
.I action
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B tulpar \-e
.I action
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manages the list of configured Tulpar Server repositories.
.TP
.B add
Appends a repository URL to the repository list file.
.TP
.B remove
Removes a repository URL from the repository list file.
.TP
.B list
Prints every configured repository, system-wide and per-user
combined.
.TP
.B update
Refreshes the cached
.B repodata.json
for every configured repository, ignoring the cache TTL.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-user
For
.B add
and
.BR remove ,
operate on the per-user repository list
.RI ( "~/.config/apg/repos" )
instead of the system-wide one
.RI ( "/etc/apg/repos" ).
When omitted, the system-wide file is used if tulpar is running as
root, and the per-user file otherwise.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apg/repos
System-wide repository list, one URL per line, lines starting with
.B #
are comments.
.TP
.I ~/.config/apg/repos
Per-user repository list, same format.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero if the requested repository could not be
added, removed, or refreshed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-search (1)
